BetterGuac changes to Apache Guacamole 1.6.0 in this package:
- guacd: FreeRDP 3 graphics (GDI) set up in the post-connect callback
  instead of before connecting, which fixes RDP crashes with FreeRDP 3;
  a -c option to read /etc/betterguac/guacd.conf. Each patched source file
  carries a change notice when built.
- guacamole-auth-jdbc-mysql: deleting user groups works, and the sign-in
  history table is written correctly (two MyBatis mapper XML files in the
  1.6.0 jar; each carries a change notice, and the jar's manifest names
  BetterGuac as the vendor of the modified build).
- Web application: BetterGuac page title, early midnight-blue page colour,
  boot loader and cache stamps in index.html (the file says so at the top).
  Nothing else in the WAR is changed. The bundled third-party libraries,
  including those under the EPL 2.0 and CDDL 1.1, are shipped unmodified;
  betterguac-setup converts the WAR and extensions from javax.* to jakarta.*
  for Tomcat 10 on the machine where it is installed, with Debian's Apache
  Tomcat migration tool (tomcat-jakartaee-migration).
- BetterGuac interface add-on and profile extension (new code).
- YAML-to-database sync tool, Activity log and schema migrations (new code).

Source code: see /usr/share/doc/betterguac/SOURCES (in the source tree:
files/SOURCES).

